Process lives in [docs/README.md](mdc:docs/README.md).

## Frontmatter

Every doc needs it. Bump `updated` when substance changes.

```yaml
---
status: canonical | draft | archived
updated: YYYY-MM-DD
decided_by: [0001, 0002]   # canonical docs only
---
```

## Routing

- Changes the **data model**, **claim contract**, **product boundary**, or **stack** → an ADR in `docs/decisions/`, using [_template.md](mdc:docs/decisions/_template.md), plus a row in [the index](mdc:docs/decisions/README.md)
- Anything smaller and unresolved → a `Q-NN` entry in [open-questions.md](mdc:docs/open-questions.md)

Never encode an undecided thing as a silent default.

## Rules

- Canonical docs explain ADRs. They do not invent binding rules.
- Reversing a decision means a new ADR that supersedes the old one. Never rewrite an accepted ADR to mean something else.
- Update affected canonical docs in the same change as the ADR.
- One place per fact — link rather than restate.
- **`docs/brainstorm/` is read-only.** Do not edit, tidy, or reconcile it.
